{{end}}
## Build

Use Windows with Visual Studio / MSBuild and the matching .NET Framework targeting
pack. Install the ESAPI SDK separately. Neither ESAPI DLLs nor documentation are
included in this project.

Set `ESAPI_HOME` to the directory that directly contains
`VMS.TPS.Common.Model.API.dll` and `VMS.TPS.Common.Model.Types.dll`.
Use a DLL directory without percent signs (`%`); the generated project rejects
these paths to avoid MSBuild interpreting them as escape sequences.

```powershell
$env:ESAPI_HOME = 'C:\path\to\ESAPI\API'
MSBuild.exe .\{{.Name}}.csproj /p:Configuration=Release
```

If generated with `--esapi-path`, the project contains that absolute path as its
default. You can override it at build time with `/p:ESAPI_HOME="C:\other\API"`.
Avoid committing a machine-specific path to a shared repository.

ESAPI DLL references have `Private=False` so MSBuild does not copy them to the
output directory. Regenerate for the desired ESAPI version and reference that
installation's DLLs; compatibility across versions has not been validated.

The project includes `Script.cs` explicitly. Add further source files to the
`.csproj` when extending the plug-in.

